.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]step\f[R] and \f[CR]continue\f[R] messages set the step mode
pre\-emptively.
They take effect at the next \f[CR]pre_command_hook\f[R] invocation, not
at an existing breakpoint pause (for that, the client sends these types
within the \f[CR]debug_wait_for_resume()\f[R] loop during a
\f[CR]break_hit\f[R] pause).
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]inspect_ast\f[R] message returns \f[CR]null\f[R] if no command
is currently pending (i.e., execution is not paused at a breakpoint).
.IP \(bu 2
All responses are sent on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R] (channel 4).
